<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0091/na_0011> <http://digistrucmed.org/recommendationStatus> "PRESENT" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0091/tu_0013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Baseline familial evaluation of SADS decedents is recommended to include taking a medical history and performing physical examination, standard- and high-precordial lead ECG, echocardiography, and exercise testing." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0091/tu_0011> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Familial evaluation of SADS decedents is recommended: • for first-degree relatives • for relatives who must carry a mutation based on analysis of the family history • for relatives with suspicious symptoms • when the decedent\\'s age is <50 years or if there are other circumstantial data or family history to suggest heritable disease." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0091/e_0069> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "VT" .
